   "id": "approach",
   "title": "Darius cuts the road, Alexander turns back",
   "time": "Early November, 333 BC",
   "narrative": "Darius brought his army north around the Amanus range and took Issus, which put it astride Alexander's supply line while the Macedonians were still south of the Pass of Jonah. On learning this, Alexander marched back up the coast in column. Darius, advancing south, got no further than the Pinarus before his scouts saw the Macedonians coming, and he drew up on the north bank of the narrow coastal plain, where his numbers counted for little.",
